!Proposed definitions

;__da__ (KOhA1): something 1. Variable that can be bound by a logical quantifier. 

ro da poi gapkla cu nitkla
%%%''Everything that goes up, comes down.''

;__de__ (KOhA1): something 2. Variable that can be bound by a logical quantifier.

su'o da su'o de gapkla gi'e stali
%%%''Something goes up somewhere and stays there.''

;__di__ (KOhA1): something 3. Variable that can be bound by a logical quantifier.

pa da broda ijo ge su'o de broda gi ro di poi broda cu du de
%%%''Exactly one x is a broda iff some y is a broda and every z that is a broda is that y.''  

!!Notes

* da, de, di are __singular__ variables when bound by singular quantifier, i.e. they take values one at a time. The quantifier indicates the number of values it can take such that with each of those values the quantified bridi is true. A variable bound by a __plural__ quantifier could take more than one value at a time to satisfy a predicate.
 